<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beagle Channel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Beagle Channel is a strait in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tierra-del-fuego">Tierra del Fuego</a> archipelago at the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hms-beagle">HMS Beagle</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">Sovereignty</a> over the islands at its eastern end was disputed between Chile and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and brought them close to war in 1978. Papal mediation averted the conflict and led to the Treaty of Peace and Friendship of 1984.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beagle-channel.jpg" alt="Beagle Channel" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ted Wakabayashi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:090111-6_Above_%E3%83%93%E3%83%BC%E3%82%B0%E3%83%AB%E6%B0%B4%E9%81%93.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
